    "id": "p14-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "For $0^\\circ<\\theta<90^\\circ$, find a value of $\\theta$ for which $\\sin\\theta=\\cos\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$45^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "The sine and cosine ratios have the same hypotenuse denominator. Equal ratios therefore mean the opposite and adjacent sides are equal. The two acute angles are equal and sum to $90^\\circ$, so $\\theta=45^\\circ$.",
